From c33303e91142aeb762ebacc3a4d01bd8176ec2c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:03:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] esp32s3: the radio as an SDR, the dump engine's receive
 side

The S3's Wi-Fi MAC has a debug dump engine. It copies the receiver's raw
baseband samples into a 64 KiB SRAM bank, one word per sample: I, Q
(negated) and the gain index, 10 bits each for I and Q. ESPARGOS esp-sdr
and esp-sdr-zephyr use it as a software-defined radio. This model follows
esp-sdr-zephyr's S3 register reference.
- DUMP_CTRL, DUMP_WRITE_INDEX and DUMP_CONFIG: a capture of COUNT words at
  80, 40 or 16 MS/s into the bank SRAM_USAGE_3 hands to the engine. DONE
  comes once the capture's time on the chip has passed in virtual time.
- The samples come from a scene: tones, noise, and AM bursts with
  Manchester data, as gbagate's rfrf_modulate() makes them (the GBA
  Wireless Adapter's radio). They are heard relative to the LO, within the
  receiver's band, and clipped at the ADC's 10 bits.
- Tuning. The analog I2C master's command words now address a register
  file for the analog blocks: a write sets a register, and a read finds it
  in bits 23:16. From it the model follows the RF PLL's fractional-N
  divider (block 0x63) and the LO's 5/6 divider (block 0x65). It also
  follows the PHY's channel hop (0x6000e150) on Wi-Fi channels.
- The AGC block (0x6001c000) keeps what the PHY writes, so the largest
  calibrated gain index reads back (82). A forced index goes into each word.

Properties on /machine/soc/sdr: scene, seed, tuned-khz, pll-khz, captures.
Not modelled yet: circular captures, transmit (the DAC), the CPU's loss of
an owned bank, gain, and the front end's readback of a forced gain (so
esp-sdr's manual gain fails its check; its AGC works).

esp32s3-sdr-test covers tuning, a tone at each rate, noise and the gain
field, bank and lane rules, and an AM burst read back bit by bit.
phy-test's "kept" list drops the command word and checks its semantics.
With ESPARGOS esp-sdr's S3 firmware at 3ab3b65, built with ESP-IDF 5.5:
SYNC, INFO and LIMITS? answer. FREQ 2437, 2432 and 1900 tune exactly; the
tones come back at their offsets and levels in CAP20 and CAP16 at all
three rates.
